# Log File Analyzer

A Python CLI tool to analyze log files, filter logs by date range, and generate summary reports in CSV format. This repo covers parsing structured logs, filtering entries by a date range, and producing a CSV summary report.

---

## Project 1: Log Parsing & Filtering

### What I Used

| Component | What It Was |
|-----------|-------------|
| Language | Python 3.6+ |
| Library | colorama |
| Input | Structured log files |
| Output | CSV summary report |
| Interface | Command-line (CLI) |
| Filter | Date-range filtering |
| Counting | Severity-level (INFO/WARN/ERROR) |

### How I Set It Up

1. Install the required dependency.

   pip3 install colorama

2. Run the analyzer with a log file and a date range.

   python3 log_analyzer.py <logfile> "<start_date>" "<end_date>" [--output <output_csv>]

3. Example command.

   python3 log_analyzer.py sample.log "2025-06-03 12:31:00" "2025-06-03 12:34:00" --output filtered_report.csv

4. Sample output.

   INFO: 1
   WARNING: 1
   ERROR: 1
   Report saved to filtered_report.csv

### How It Works

1. Reads and parses the log file
2. Filters logs within the specified date range
3. Counts log entries by their level
4. Displays a color-coded summary in the terminal
5. Saves the summary as a CSV report

